    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T20:12:56Z",
    "body": "Addition from the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat): \"Engagement doesnt seem todo what it should either, these should be related to a degree.\"\n\nScope added to this issue: the engagement setting (optimal load / engagement angle) also appears to have no effect on the generated path. Stepover and engagement describe the same thing from two sides (radial width of cut and the arc of the tool in contact), so check them together:\n- which of the two the generator actually reads, and whether the other is ignored or overwritten;\n- whether one is derived from the other, and if so that editing either one updates the path and the other field shows the derived value;\n- when both are set and disagree, which wins, and that the operation says so instead of silently using one.\n\nDone means (added): a test changes the engagement value and asserts the path changes or the value is refused by name; the relation between stepover and engagement is one rule, stated in the operation's tooltip or message and pinned by a test.\n",
