    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T20:14:17Z",
    "body": "Addition from the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat): \"there is also \"optimal load\" on passes page.. not sure which is actually winning and where they apply\"\n\nScope added: three fields now describe the radial load - stepover, engagement, and \"optimal load\" on the Passes page - and the user cannot tell which one the generator uses or for which operations each applies.\n\nTo settle in this issue:\n- for each operation, list which of the three it reads at generate and which it ignores;\n- one rule for precedence where more than one is shown, stated in the UI (tooltip or a line under the field), with the losing field shown as derived or disabled rather than editable and ignored;\n- a field an operation does not use is not shown on that operation's pages.\n\nDone means (added): a test per operation changes each shown load field and asserts the path changes or the value is refused by name; no operation shows a load field that has no effect.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
